    "title": "Galen College of Nursing alumni and staff fill Thanksgiving baskets for students - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rhian Lowndes ,\n1 days ago\nROANOKE COUNTY, Va. ( WFXR ) – Galen College of Nursing Roanoke put together Thanksgiving baskets to its students in need this holiday season.\nDean Kimberly Brown says many of their student nurses are single moms, working to improve their lives.\nOlde Salem Brewing Company “Pouring it Forward” with the Life Ring Foundation “They chose to add three days of school on top of family, home and several jobs and we’re here to help them persist, not just academically but any way we can,” she said.\nStaff and faculty packed 25 baskets for students with the help of the local Food Lion, which contributed turkeys when they heard about the initiative.\nThe college also has a pantry for its 300 students in case they need it. Brown says members of the public can bring donations if they’d like to help.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFXRtv.\n3",
